WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.400
24 years and 50,000 flights ago, the China Clipper left San Francisco, headed westward

00:08.400 --> 00:11.400
on the first scheduled flight across any major ocean.

00:11.400 --> 00:24.120
The classic flying boat was luxurious for its day, not bad even by current standards.

00:24.120 --> 00:29.440
Over the then under construction Golden Gate, westward toward Hawaii, Guam, Wake Island,

00:29.440 --> 00:31.560
Destination Manila, and history.

00:31.560 --> 00:37.320
Today, 50,000 Trans-Pacific flights later, the 50th State Hawaii celebrates the historic

00:37.320 --> 00:38.320
anniversary.

00:38.320 --> 00:43.160
The hula is unchanged, but the Trans-Pacific run is no longer an adventure, it's routine

00:43.160 --> 00:48.160
in less than a generation.

00:48.160 --> 00:57.720
A fashion holiday on the fly, arriving in the colorful Netherlands Antilles for an island

00:57.720 --> 01:02.360
interlude, the gals are traveling light, for their wardrobes relying not on quantity but

01:02.360 --> 01:07.280
on the versatility of the new Canadian synthetic to get the most fashion mileage with the least

01:07.280 --> 01:08.280
luggage.

01:08.280 --> 01:09.280
Can do?

01:09.280 --> 01:10.280
Uh-huh.

01:10.280 --> 01:14.640
Starting with coffee on the terrace, overlooking Curaçao's rare blend of 17th century Holland

01:14.640 --> 01:20.260
and West Indian foliage, the gals are relaxing in cool house coats, full length and shorty

01:20.260 --> 01:30.760
models respectively.

01:30.760 --> 01:35.360
Quick change for a picnic on the unsurpassable beach at Aruba, a brief interlude, bikinis

01:35.360 --> 01:40.160
for every taste, lace embroidered or boldly striped, and tailored from the same miracle

01:40.160 --> 01:49.880
fiber as the rest of the gals travel wardrobe.

01:49.880 --> 01:55.320
Young sees the cycle complete on the terrace in cocktail dresses of Rivoline and pretty

01:55.320 --> 02:01.920
as naturally a picture, according to a careful observer with an eye for attractive compositions,

02:01.920 --> 02:15.720
namely me.

02:15.720 --> 02:20.200
From sunshine and warm weather and the zoo comes into its own, the official greeters

02:20.200 --> 02:24.200
in full dress, of course, are on the job, conscious of their importance and out to make

02:24.200 --> 02:32.760
a splash for the benefit of the visiting kids.

02:32.760 --> 02:40.360
The zoo's own young ones are up to their own brand of mischief.

02:40.360 --> 03:00.560
Now, this is what you call monkey business, this character really swings.

03:00.560 --> 03:07.640
Even the lioness gets to feeling kittenish.

03:07.640 --> 03:15.920
The old man disapproves, grouchy as a bear, whatever the season.

03:15.920 --> 03:20.400
The big cats are downright playful, but the kitten, well, she figures the tigers are in

03:20.400 --> 03:21.880
another league altogether.

03:21.880 --> 03:26.400
It could only happen in the children's zoo, where all the animals are friendly and the

03:26.400 --> 03:30.800
kids have a ball amongst the mixed up four-legged panhandlers.

03:30.800 --> 03:36.480
Kids meet kid, who's kidding who?

03:36.480 --> 03:52.840
Yeah, they're making extra money.

03:52.840 --> 04:05.600
Here's one of those people.

